{"Title":"An Act relative to timely retirement payment","BillNumber":"H2682","DocketNumber":"HD2925","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"T_V1","Name":"Tommy Vitolo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_V1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:02:21.623"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"T_V1","Name":"Tommy Vitolo","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/T_V1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-18T10:02:21.6233333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H2682/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Vitolo of Brookline, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 2682) of Tommy Vitolo relative to timely retirement payments to retiring public employees.  Public Service.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Paragraph (B) of subdivision (1) of Section 13 of Chapter 32 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by adding the following after the words “allowance becomes effective.”, the following:\r\n\t“In the event circumstances beyond the retirement board’s control prevent the calculation of the full monthly payment by the first such full payment date, the retirement board shall pay 90% of its estimated full monthly payment until such time as the circumstances beyond the retirement board’s control are corrected. On an annual basis, the retirement board will notify the House and the Senate of all circumstances beyond the retirement board’s control that prevented the calculation of the full monthly payment by the first such full payment date.”\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Favorable","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}